      "id": "1utthv9",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. INTRODUCTION TO ECONOMIC SECTORS"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Primary Sector directly utilizes natural resources, encompassing agriculture, forestry, fishing, and mining.",
        "Secondary Sector covers manufacturing, industrial production, and processing activities that convert raw materials into finished goods.",
        "Tertiary Sector produces services rather than goods, supporting both primary and secondary sectors through transport, banking, and trade.",
        "Organised sector enterprises follow government rules and offer formal employment with social security, whereas unorganised sectors lack formal job security.",
        "Public sector units are government-owned aimed at public welfare, while private sector enterprises are individually owned aimed at profit."
      ],
      "id": "edzbpik"
    },
