      "content": "8. SECTORAL SHIFT IN INDIA"
    },
    {
      "type": "examAlert",
      "items": [
        "Questions frequently distinguish Primary, Secondary, and Tertiary sectors by their core activities (e.g., farming vs. manufacturing vs. banking).",
        "SSC exams frequently test characteristics of Unorganised sector employment conditions, such as lack of paid leave and job security.",
        "Key difference between Public and Private sectors lies in ownership and primary objective: social welfare vs. profit motive.",
        "Sectoral shift in India highlights a direct transition of GDP share from agriculture to services without significant industrial growth."
      ],
